{title: Seas of Crimson}
{artist: D. Bashta, Bill Johnson}
{key: A}

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]For every curse, [E]You’re the [A]cure
[A]For every sickness, [D]You’re the [A]healer
For every [F#m]storm, You’re the [D]calm
For all that’s [A]lost, Oh [E]what a [A]Savior

{comment: Chorus}
[E]Hallelujah
Death is [F#m]beaten
Christ is [D]risen from the [A]grave
[E]Hallejuah, it is [F#m]finished
All to [D]You, the [E]highest [A]praise

{comment: Verse 2}
[A]On that cross of [E]Calvary[A]
Every burden has [D]been [A]defeated
And every [F#m]wretched heart [D]redeemed
You drown our [A]sins in [E]seas of [A]crimson
And every [F#m]wretched heart [D]redeemed
You drown our [A]sins in [E]seas of [A]crimson

{comment: Verse 3}
[A]On that day of utmost [E]glory[A]
All of darkness [D]cannot [A]tarry
And every [F#m]shackle come [D]undone
My solid [A]Rock, Thine [E]is the [A]Kingdom
And every [F#m]shackle come [D]undone
My solid [A]Rock, Thine [E]is the [A]Kingdom

{comment: Bridge}
[F#m]Where there was sin, Your love [D]rushed in
[A]Where sin runs deep, Your grace [E]runs deeper
[F#m]For all enslaved, the ransom [D]paid
[A]Hope of the world, all hail the [E]power
